 "scope_and_limits": [
  "One frozen local release binary, synthetic generated zero-byte metadata, no cloud credentials, content reads or foreground provider requests.",
  "TMPDIR and SQLITE_TMPDIR were placed explicitly on Btrfs and verified in the live environment. No concurrent local compilation or other benchmarks ran.",
  "first_entry seconds measure only OPENDIR to the first returned entry of the giant directory. Traversal seconds measure a whole pass, including the complete enumeration and deferred release.",
  "At the first entry the published prefix holds 130 of 500,002 entries and 8,493 logical bytes; the remaining entries are produced while the reader consumes that prefix.",
  "The first-entry improvement is confirmed by a controlled frozen-binary pair on one idle machine: baseline 8.80-10.76 s against 4.33-5.23 ms, with no overlap between the distributions.",
  "The same controlled pair shows whole-pass traversal unchanged, medians 10.585 s baseline against 10.232 s new. The higher traversal seconds against the 2026-09-07 artifact were a session difference; that earlier pair was never controlled and is kept only for context.",
  "Post-invalidation RSS still rises across the three passes (18.3 / 33.9 / 43.4 MiB). This run does not establish a memory plateau and does not close the namespace capacity gate.",
  "No mapped content, writable overlays, deep aliases, held descriptors, desktop applications, real-provider acceptance or 24-hour sustained operation."
 ],
